Subject: [PATCH] vLLM 0.25: native W4A8 (mxfp4-weight + FP8-act) via AITER FlyDSL afp8_wfp4

Before this patch, the quark OCP-MX scheme w_mxfp4_a_fp8 (W4A8) had only one native
vLLM backend: AITER_MXFP4_FP8 -> AiterW4A8ExpertsMonolithic, which calls the gpt-oss
triton kernel moe_gemm_a8w4 and rejects any activation other than SWIGLUOAI
(aiter_mxfp4_w4a8_moe.py:227). Qwen3-VL uses SILU, so the oracle fell through to NONE
-> EMULATION (OCP_MXQuantizationEmulationTritonExperts), which dequantizes weights on
the fly and is very slow (~3.7 QPS), even though W4A8 is the only quant that passes the
MLPerf Category-F1 gate (>= 0.7824; W4A4 ~0.77 fails).

AITER main (>= 0.1.17.dev, d7c40514) adds a native FlyDSL MoE kernel family
"afp8_wfp4" (FP8 activation x MXFP4 weight) reachable through aiter.fused_moe on gfx950.
It is SILU-native and uses the same gate/up-interleaved a16w4 weight layout as the
existing W4A16 path (aiter fused_moe.py use_mxfp4_flydsl gate). aiter's own a8w4
correctness test on Qwen shapes agrees with the bf16 reference to logits_diff ~1e-3.

This patch re-points the AITER_MXFP4_FP8 backend at the general AiterExperts
(rocm_aiter_moe.rocm_aiter_fused_experts -> aiter.fused_moe) instead of the SILU-rejecting
monolithic, and teaches that path the W4A8 combo:
  * oracle/mxfp4.py backend_to_kernel_cls: AITER_MXFP4_FP8 -> AiterExperts.
  * oracle/mxfp4.py weight prep: replace the triton_kernels swizzle with the W4A16-style
    gate/up-interleaved shuffle_weight_a16w4 / shuffle_scale_a16w4. Qwen quark w13 is
    stored CONTIGUOUS [gate; up] (unlike the gpt-oss W4A16 checkpoint which is already
    interleaved), so we do NOT de-interleave first. Static FP8 input scales are reduced
    to a per-tensor scalar and written back to the layer so they become a1_scale/a2_scale.
  * rocm_aiter_moe.py AiterExperts._supports_quant_scheme: allow (kMxfp4Static,
    kFp8StaticTensorSym); rocm_aiter_fused_experts: use_mxfp4_w4a8 -> quant_method
    BLOCK_1X32 + gate_mode INTERLEAVE.
  * quark_moe.py: treat AITER_MXFP4_FP8 as a standard-param (not triton_kernels) backend
    in _setup_kernel + get_fused_moe_quant_config, and set is_shuffled=True (FlyDSL gate).

The FusedMoEQuantConfig plumbing (use_mxfp4_w4a8, mxfp4_w4a8_moe_quant_config,
make_mxfp4_moe_quant_config -> AITER_MXFP4_FP8) already existed in vLLM 0.25 and is unchanged.

REQUIRED runtime env: AITER_BF16_FP8_MOE_BOUND=0. aiter fused_moe.py:609 uses bf16
activation (the a16w4 CK kernel, which does NOT exist on gfx950 -> "Unsupported kernel
config for moe heuristic dispatch") for token counts below this bound, and FP8 (FlyDSL
afp8_wfp4) at/above it. Setting the bound to 0 forces FP8 for all M, which is exactly the
W4A8 scheme and keeps every shape on the native FlyDSL kernel (avoids a decode-time crash
during cudagraph capture). Set via configs/benchmark.yaml env: block or
`+env.AITER_BF16_FP8_MOE_BOUND=0`.

Result on Qwen3-VL-235B W4A8 (w4a8-base + FP8-last-16), 0.25 + AITER main:
accuracy_verification_8k Category-F1 = 0.7837 (PASSES the 0.7824 gate), served natively.

See docs/fp8-last-n-runbook.md.

